# Detailed guide

A detailed guide supports a specific task that needs substantial, maintained instructions. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/detailed-guide/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## When to use it

Use it for installing the companion, upgrading a supported version or recovering a known configuration. Start with the intended outcome, supported baseline and prerequisites. Place steps in the order people must perform them, with checks at the points where mistakes would otherwise go unnoticed.

## Structure and behaviour

Include a contents list, meaningful headings, concise code blocks where necessary, and verified recovery information. Publish a real first-publication date and maintain dated change notes. In current publishing metadata, page-history entries belong to page_history; do not build new guidance around the removed published-dates component.

## Home Assistant boundary

The guide is instructional content, not an automated installer. Never imply that reading a step completed it. Do not invent a supported Home Assistant version, release URL or backup location. Keep security-sensitive credentials and private household details out of public examples.

