## Acceptance checks

- Instructions match the version being documented.
- Each potentially disruptive step has a practical validation point.
- Code and links are verified against the package.
- Change notes explain user-visible changes rather than every internal edit.

Check the examples at narrow widths, with a keyboard and without JavaScript. Test a production implementation against its actual data and permissions before calling it supported.

## Sources and maintenance

Reviewed against the official guidance on 11 November 2026. The [source and migration record](../source-history.html) separates the Publishing Design Guide from the component gem and records the metadata-history migration. Use local typography and colour roles with the household’s optional identity; official GOV.UK marks, analytics and account services are not part of this adaptation.

